[{"slug": "vermont-property-tax-guide", "title": "Vermont Property Tax Guide: Appeals, Exemptions and Selling With Tax Due", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Vermont Property Tax Guide: Appeals, Exemptions and Selling With Tax Due</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Vermont</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Vermont Property Tax Guide: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Vermont Property Tax Guide sale</li><li>Turn the Vermont Property Tax Guide offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Vermont House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Vermont property tax is assessed and collected at the local level, and owners can appeal an assessment.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Listers hear persons aggrieved by their appraisals on or before May 20 (from day to day thereafter); such hearings are not held later than June 2. (32 V.S.A. \u00a7 4221; <a href='https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/section/32/129/04221' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A person aggrieved by the listers&#x27; final decision may appeal in writing to the board of civil authority within 14 days after the date of notice, by lodging the appeal with the town clerk. (32 V.S.A. \u00a7 4404; <a href='https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/section/32/131/04404' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The town clerk calls a board of civil authority meeting to hear appeals not later than 14 days after the last date allowed for notice of appeal. (32 V.S.A. \u00a7 4404; <a href='https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/section/32/131/04404' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Appeal to either the Director of Property Valuation and Review or the Superior Court is commenced by filing a notice of appeal under V.R.C.P. 74 within 30 days after entry of the board of civil authority&#x27;s decision. (32 V.S.A. \u00a7 4461; <a href='https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/section/32/131/04461' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Delinquent taxpayer must receive certified-mail written notice of the date and place of the tax sale at least 30 days prior. (32 V.S.A. \u00a7 5252(3); <a href='https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/section/32/133/05252' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>The owner, lienholder or mortgagee may redeem within one year from the day of sale by paying the sale price plus interest at 1% per month or fraction thereof. (32 V.S.A. \u00a7 5260(a); <a href='https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/section/32/133/05260' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Vermont?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Vermont houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/vermont-estate-tax/'>Vermont Estate and Inheritance Tax</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-vermont/'>We buy houses in Vermont</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://tax.vermont.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Vermont Department of Taxes</a></li><li><a href='https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Vermont Statutes</a></li><li><a href='https://www.vermontjudiciary.org/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Vermont Judiciary</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Vermont Property Tax Guide, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Vermont\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-vermont/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Vermont Property Tax Guide: Appeals\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/vermont-property-tax-guide/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Vermont Property Tax Guide: Appeals", "rank_math_description": "Vermont property tax: appeals, exemptions, delinquent tax and selling a house with tax due. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "vermont property tax"}, {"slug": "vermont-estate-tax", "title": "Vermont Estate and Inheritance Tax: What Heirs Owe When Selling", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Vermont Estate and Inheritance Tax: What Heirs Owe When Selling</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Vermont</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Vermont Estate and Inheritance Tax: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Vermont Estate and Inheritance Tax sale</li><li>Turn the Vermont Estate and Inheritance Tax offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Vermont House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>This guide covers what official sources say about Vermont estate and inheritance tax.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Vermont imposes an estate tax of 16% of the excess over $5,000,000 of the Vermont taxable estate; none under $5,000,000. (32 V.S.A. \u00a7 7442a; <a href='https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/section/32/190/07442a' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>In 2026 the Legislature raised the estate tax filing threshold to $5 million to match the payment threshold (effective June 18, 2026). (Estate Tax | Department of Taxes; <a href='https://tax.vermont.gov/individuals/estate-tax' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Form EST-191 must be filed if the decedent had an interest in Vermont property and the federal gross estate plus federal adjusted taxable gifts within two years of death exceeds $5 million, or a federal Form 706 is required. (Estate Tax | Department of Taxes; <a href='https://tax.vermont.gov/individuals/estate-tax' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Vermont?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Vermont houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/vermont-property-tax-guide/'>Vermont Property Tax Guide: Appeals</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-vermont/'>We buy houses in Vermont</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://tax.vermont.gov/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Vermont Department of Taxes</a></li><li><a href='https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Vermont Statutes</a></li><li><a href='https://www.vermontjudiciary.org/' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Vermont Judiciary</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Vermont Estate and Inheritance Tax, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Vermont\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-vermont/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Vermont Estate and Inheritance Tax\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/vermont-estate-tax/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Vermont Estate and Inheritance Tax", "rank_math_description": "Vermont estate and inheritance tax rules and how they affect heirs selling an inherited house. Official sources only.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "vermont estate tax"}]